# E10 Iterated Prisoner Dilemma: sequential, fixed order, so the C# guarantees the order of every line (exact trace,
# level (a)): "line" checks the whole trace, the other facts each kind: rounds, plays, outcomes and the end in
# sequence, final points of each prisoner.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact line ^(.+)$
fact round ^Round (\d+)$
fact message ^\t\[([\w-]+) -> ([\w-]+)\]: (.*)$
fact points ^\[([\w-]+)\]: I have (-?\d+) points$
same line seq
same round seq
same message seq
same points seq
check round count == 10
# per sender: each prisoner plays 10 times, the police answers 20 times, the environment ends the game twice
check message count == 42
check message distinct(0) == 4
